# chora-web local configuration.
#
# The Angular app reads its config from src/environments/*.ts at BUILD time
# (angular.json fileReplacements) — there is no runtime env injection. This
# file documents the knobs that exist; copy to .env for reference, but the
# values that actually reach the browser are the compiled environment files.
#
#   bffBaseUrl      — the chora-gateway BFF origin. Default builds point at
#                      the deployed gateway (https://api.chora.site); the
#                      `local` configuration points at http://localhost:8093
#                      (the gateway's host port in the compose stack).
#   wsBaseUrl       — WebSocket realtime channel origin (same gateway).
#   production       — true for deployed builds, false for local dev.
#
# Auth: username/password only. The login screen posts credentials to
# POST {bffBaseUrl}/api/v1/auth/session/mint. The seed admin account in the
# compose stack is `admin` / `admin` (CHORA_SEED_ADMIN_USERNAME / _PASSWORD).
#
# Docker: the image serves the built SPA via nginx and reverse-proxies /api
# to the gateway — no env vars required at runtime.
